{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented on change 1618 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1618). close_precheck now hard-fails a --class duplicate close with no usable replacement link, naming the exact 'rebar link <id> <canonical> duplicates' command, and distinguishes a dead/archived named target from having named none. Scoped to 'duplicate' alone per the operator decision; not_a_bug and escalated keep the prior fallthrough since neither owes a duplicates link. Link EXISTENCE only is required — a regression test pins that a CLOSED canonical still takes the disposition path. New decision points live in a guard function because _completion_precheck sits at its ceiling in the shrink-only complexity baseline. 10 new unit tests; verified RED (3 fail without the fix). Gates: make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS, tests/unit -k close 236 passed, tests/interfaces -k 'close or transition' 160 passed. LLM-Review +1 (PASS, 2 advisory)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786505474407926001,"uuid":"cdd790c0-ec38-4ac7-9953-f9f26ecc0b41"}